{"ts":"2026-09-05T19:06:25.757Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bc5f6d24074543521094561e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Report and scope\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1205\n\nClarify the published distinction between root help flags and inherited host-reserved subcommand flags. The existing preflight contract deliberately validates SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS; root --explain and command-local --explain can represent separate parser positions. Confirm runtime behavior and expose a typed machine-readable reservation scope for package authors without abruptly breaking existing pm-context or pm-brief commands.\n\n## Reported reproduction\n\n## Summary\n\n`--explain` is declared host-owned in the machine-readable contracts, but an extension that declares the same spelling on one of its commands activates successfully and **wins** at runtime. The contract and the runtime disagree, so whether an extension may declare a given host flag depends on which flag it is, with nothing in the published data saying so.\n\n## What the contracts say\n\n```js\nimport { GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS, SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS } from \"@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/contracts\";\n// → {\"flag\":\"--explain\",\"value_type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Expand root help with command guidance.\"}\n// 43 host-owned contracts in total\n```\n\n## What the runtime does\n\n`pm-context` declares exactly that spelling on its own command:\n\n```js\n{ long: \"--explain\", description: \"Explain emitted items with ranks/scores …\", type: \"boolean\" }\n```\n\nInstalled as an extension on **2026.9.5**, it activates with no error or warning, the command registers, and the extension's flag takes effect — the host's root-help expansion never happens:\n\n```\n$ pm package install pm-context-2026.8.31.tgz\nok: true\n$ pm --help --all | grep context-pack\n  context-pack [options]   Generate a durable pm context pack for handoffs and reviews.\n$ pm context-pack --explain --limit 2\n# pm context explain\nGenerated: 2026-09-05T18:20:14.790Z\nModel: default-weighted-v1\n…\n```\n\n## Why this is a problem rather than a nicety\n\nOther flags in this same contract list *are* enforced: declaring one aborts registration at the offending command, and — as we have been bitten by before — silently drops the extension's **later** sibling commands. So the list is load-bearing for some entries and inert for others, and an extension author cannot tell which from the published data.\n\nThe two failure directions:\n\n1. **Today**: an extension shadows a documented global. A user who has that extension installed gets different behaviour from `--explain` than the host documents, with nothing reporting the conflict.\n2. **Tomorrow**: if enforcement is extended to cover `--explain`, every extension currently declaring it loses a command at activation — silently, and possibly along with unrelated sibling commands registered after it.\n\nWe currently have two packages declaring it (`pm-context`, `pm-brief`), both passing CI, both exposed to (2).\n\n## Expected\n\nPick one and make the contracts say which:\n\n- **Enforce it** — refuse activation with the same clear error used for the other host-owned flags, so the collision surfaces at install time rather than as divergent runtime behaviour; or\n- **Mark it advisory** — add a field to the contract entries distinguishing *reserved and enforced* from *reserved by convention*, so a package-side gate can check the enforced subset instead of the whole list.\n\nThe second matters because the natural way to build such a gate is to iterate `GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS` and forbid every entry — which is what one of our packages does. That gate is correct against the published contract and currently forces a user-visible flag rename for a collision the runtime does not actually have.\n\n## Environment\n\n@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, Node 22/26, Linux. Extension installed from a packed tarball into a fresh `pm init` tracker.\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nIntake only in PR #1204. This item remains open and unclaimed; no implementation or reproduction success is asserted. Implement through the public SDK with thin CLI adapters and executable negative controls before closing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-2h8t6y"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1205: Declare root-only versus inherited extension flag reservation scope"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Clarify the published distinction between root help flags and inherited host-reserved subcommand flags. The existing preflight contract deliberately validates SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS; root --explain and command-local --explain can represent separate parser positions. Confirm runtime behavior and expose a typed machine-readable reservation scope for package authors without abruptly breaking existing pm-context or pm-brief commands."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-05T19:06:25.757Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-05T19:06:25.757Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Public contract data distinguishes root-only flags from enforced inherited subcommand reservations; Blueprint lint, runtime activation, and package author checks consume the same documented scope; Packed extension tests exercise root --explain and command-local --explain without dropping healthy sibling commands; Any compatibility change has an explicit migration contract and does not silently quarantine existing valid packages"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Reduce recovery ambiguity and preserve trustworthy project context for agents"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"A reproducible SDK contract with actionable CLI recovery and regression evidence"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"New user report GH-1205 during PR #1204 final integration"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.9.5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk/extensions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1205","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:25.757Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"global","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-huolbk","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:25.757Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ugqx","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:25.757Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:25.757Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"\"text=Duplicate-check evidence: strict complete all-status corpus contained 2642 items, including terminal history; exact GitHub issue URL was absent. Request-specific search and current open/in_progress inventories were read. Full live predecessor pm-huolbk and parent pm-ugqx metadata plus verified history were inspected. This report extends a